---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { T } from "../../lib/pages/resources-network";
import CtaBand from "../../components/CtaBand.astro";
---

<BaseLayout route="resources/network">
  <div class="crumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span class="crumb-sep">/</span>Resources<span class="crumb-sep">/</span>Network requirements</div>
    <div class="pageinfo"><span class="tag t-tpl">T8</span><span class="tag t-open">OPEN</span><span class="tag t-gated">PUBLISH GATE: source doc marked internal — security team sign-off required</span></div>
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:flex-end;justify-content:space-between;gap:18px;flex-wrap:wrap"><h1 class="pg" style="margin-bottom:6px">Network requirements, in full.</h1><a class="btn" style="background:#2e7a4f;border:1px solid #7ce3a8;color:#eafff3;white-space:nowrap" href="https://documentation.mersive.com/en/mcs/network-requirements.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener" title="The canonical network requirements on documentation.mersive.com">Download &#8595;</a></div>
    <p class="note">[PDF export URL: confirm with docs team &mdash; this button currently points at the HTML page, not a PDF]</p>
    <p class="dek">Every port, protocol, and endpoint Mersive Polaris uses, exactly as our own diagnostic tool validates them. Your firewall team can read this page once and approve the deployment. Nothing is hidden behind a support ticket.</p>

    <section class="sect reveal tight">
      <div class="kicker">Outbound · cloud services</div>
      <h2>Pod and client to the internet.</h2>
      <p class="sdek">All endpoints require outbound HTTPS (TCP 443) from both the Pod VLAN and the client VLAN. This is signaling, licensing, and management traffic. Meeting pixels are not routed through these endpoints on a shared network.</p>
      <Fragment set:html={T(["Port","Protocol","Endpoint","Purpose"],[
        ["TCP 443","HTTPS/TLS","app.mersive.com","Portal / signaling server"],
        ["TCP 443","HTTPS/TLS","display.mersive.com","Mersive display app"],
        ["TCP 443","HTTPS/TLS","mcsapi.mersive.com","Polaris API service"],
        ["TCP 443","HTTPS/TLS","webrtc.mersive.com","WebRTC signaling server"],
        ["TCP 443","HTTPS/TLS","hosted.mender.io","Update server"],
        ["TCP 443","HTTPS/TLS","hosted-mender-artifacts.s3.amazonaws.com","Update artifacts (AWS S3)"],
        ["TCP 443","HTTPS/TLS","c271964d41749feb10da762816c952ee.r2.cloudflarestorage.com","Update artifacts (Cloudflare R2) [validated host; if ops wants the *.r2.cloudflarestorage.com wildcard for bucket-change resilience, decide that deliberately and footnote it]"],
        ["TCP 443","HTTPS/TLS","app.launchdarkly.com","Feature flags"],
        ["TCP 443","HTTPS/TLS","clientstream.launchdarkly.com","Feature flag streaming"],
        ["TCP 443","HTTPS/TLS","events.launchdarkly.com","Feature flag events"],
        ["TCP 443","HTTPS/TLS","firestore.googleapis.com","Real-time state sync"],
        ["TCP 443","HTTPS/TLS","firebasestorage.googleapis.com","Storage &amp; licensing info"],
        ["TCP 443","HTTPS/TLS","identitytoolkit.googleapis.com","Authentication (identity)"],
        ["TCP 443","HTTPS/TLS","securetoken.googleapis.com","Authentication (token)"]
      ])} />
    </section>

    <section class="sect reveal tight">
      <div class="kicker">Outbound · UDP</div>
      <h2>Time and NAT traversal.</h2>
      <p class="sdek">These must not be blocked by stateful firewalls or NAT policies. Clock drift over two minutes breaks TLS certificate validation.</p>
      <Fragment set:html={T(["Port","Protocol","Endpoint","Purpose"],[
        ["UDP 123","NTP","ntp.mersive.com","Time sync (fallback: time.google.com)"],
        ["UDP 19302","STUN","stun.l.google.com","WebRTC NAT traversal"],
        ["UDP 19302","STUN","stun1.l.google.com","NAT traversal (backup)"]
      ])} />
    </section>

    <section class="sect reveal tight">
      <div class="kicker">Local · discovery</div>
      <h2>Multicast on the Pod VLAN.</h2>
      <p class="sdek">Required for AirPlay and Google Cast device discovery. If multicast is filtered, native casting discovery will not function; web-join is unaffected.</p>
      <Fragment set:html={T(["Port","Protocol","Multicast address","Purpose"],[
        ["UDP 5353","mDNS","224.0.0.251","AirPlay + Mersive discovery (Bonjour)"],
        ["UDP 1900","SSDP","239.255.255.250","Google Cast / UPnP discovery"]
      ])} />
    </section>

    <section class="sect reveal tight">
      <div class="kicker">Inter-VLAN · pod-local ports</div>
      <h2>Client VLAN to Pod VLAN.</h2>
      <p class="sdek">When Pods live on their own VLAN, inter-VLAN rules must permit traffic to these Pod-side ports for casting and sharing.</p>
      <Fragment set:html={T(["Port","Protocol","Purpose"],[
        ["TCP 7000","AirPlay","AirPlay service"],
        ["TCP 7001","AirPlay","AirPlay mirroring"],
        ["TCP 7100","AirPlay","AirPlay control channel"],
        ["TCP 7236","Miracast","Miracast RTSP / control"],
        ["TCP 8008","Google Cast","Cast HTTP"],
        ["TCP 8009","Google Cast","Cast TLS"],
        ["TCP 8443","Mersive","Mersive secure service"],
        ["TCP 443","HTTPS","Reachability (diagnostic validation)"]
      ])} />
      <Fragment set:html={T(["Port range","Protocol","Direction","Purpose"],[
        ["UDP 40000–49999","RTP/RTCP","Client VLAN ⇄ Pod VLAN","WebRTC media stream (screen sharing), bidirectional"]
      ])} />
      <p class="note">The required production range is UDP 40000–49999. The diagnostic tool samples across that range and also spot-checks ports on either side of it (32768–39999 and 50000–65535) to catch partial blocks that would otherwise look like a clean pass.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="sect reveal tight">
      <div class="kicker">Reference architecture</div>
      <h2>The recommended VLAN design.</h2>
      <p class="sdek">Standard deployment separates client devices (VLAN 10) from Pods (VLAN 20) with a stateful firewall between them. Seven pinhole rules cover everything above. This is the page your network engineer approves; IT stays in control of how sessions connect.</p>
      <Fragment set:html={T(["Traffic flow","Ports","Purpose"],[
        ["VLAN 10 (client) → internet","TCP 443 outbound","The 14 cloud endpoints above"],
        ["VLAN 20 (pod) → internet","TCP 443 outbound","The 14 cloud endpoints above"],
        ["VLAN 10 → VLAN 20","TCP 7000–7001, 7100, 7236, 8008–8009, 8443","Casting and discovery"],
        ["VLAN 10 ⇄ VLAN 20","UDP 40000–49999","WebRTC media (screen sharing)"],
        ["Both VLANs → internet","UDP 19302 outbound","STUN (NAT traversal)"],
        ["Both VLANs → internet","UDP 123 outbound","NTP time sync"],
        ["VLAN 20 (local)","UDP 5353, 1900 multicast","mDNS / SSDP discovery"]
      ])} />
      <p class="note">[Asset owed: the one-page flows diagram drawn from this table — SE team. This page is the data; the diagram is the picture. Interim reference below.]</p>
      <figure class="prodimg reveal" style="max-width:620px"><img src="data:image/webp;base64," alt="Mersive Pod connection diagram" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Pod connection diagram from the hardware library. Production replaces this with the engineer-grade flows-and-ports diagram (asset G3).</figcaption></figure>
    </section>

    <section class="sect reveal tight">
      <div class="kicker">Validate it</div>
      <h2>The diagnostic tool.</h2>
      <p class="sdek">mersive_network_diag.py validates every requirement on this page from any machine on the target network. Python 3.7+, standard library only, nothing to install. [PUBLISH GATE unresolved: the tool&rsquo;s README is marked INTERNAL USE ONLY and the download link is a placeholder — clear it for public distribution or this section does not publish.]</p>
      <Fragment set:html={T(["Command","What it does"],[
        ["python3 mersive_network_diag.py","Opens the diagnostic in your browser and runs the full check"],
        ["python3 mersive_network_diag.py --quick","Five-second smoke test: DNS, STUN, NAT, and NTP"],
        ["python3 mersive_network_diag.py --cloud-only","DNS and TLS checks against the 14 cloud endpoints"],
        ["python3 mersive_network_diag.py --pod-ip 10.0.2.50","Adds a cross-VLAN probe against a specific pod"],
        ["python3 mersive_network_diag.py --json","Machine-readable output"],
        ["python3 mersive_network_diag.py --send-to-support","Saves the report and opens your email client, addressed to support"]
      ])} />
      <p class="note">On a VLAN-separated deployment, run it once from the client VLAN and once from the pod VLAN. Cross-VLAN checks need a client-VLAN run pointed at a pod-VLAN address.</p>
      <p class="note"><b>NAT symmetry:</b> symmetric NAT silently breaks WebRTC even when every port appears open, because each destination sees a different external port and no direct path can be formed. The tool validates NAT type against both STUN servers and reports symmetric NAT as a critical failure. <a href="/platform/cross-network">How cross-network sharing connects →</a></p>
    </section>
    <CtaBand variant="platform" />
</BaseLayout>
